# Vulnerabilities tools/ci/scan_images.sh accepts for now. Each entry expires: after its date Trivy
# reports it again and the image-scan job fails, so every exception gets looked at again.
# Format: one ID per line, optionally `exp:YYYY-MM-DD`.

# BASH32_IMAGE (mirror.gcr.io/library/bash:3.2@sha256:2556c2da19c3..., alpine 3.22.8) has
# libcrypto3 / libssl3 3.5.9-r0. OpenSSL fixed this QUIC denial of service in 3.5.9-r2, Alpine
# ships it, but Docker Hub had not rebuilt any bash:3.2 tag by 2026-11-26, so no fixed digest
# exists. The image only runs ai-task's shell tests (job ai-task-portable, which also upgrades
# both packages at start); nothing there uses OpenSSL's QUIC code. Decided by Jim on 2026-11-26.
# Remove this entry when BASH32_IMAGE moves to a rebuilt digest.
CVE-2026-124709 exp:2026-12-10
